Reason:
The test case `testSaslPlainServerBadPassword` was expecting an exact match of the error message when authentication failed. If the error message format changed or included additional information, the assertion would fail, leading to a lack of flexibility in the test.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
String message = e.getMessage();
assertContains("PLAIN auth failed", message);
assertContains("wrong password", message);
```
Reason:
The patch modifies the assertion logic to check for the presence of key phrases in the error message rather than an exact match. This allows the test to pass even if the error message format changes, thus improving the flexibility and robustness of the test case.


